kind: vulnerability
title: "Cisco Catalyst SD-WAN CLI privilege escalation CVE-2026-20245, exploited as a zero-day after attackers gained administrator access"
headline: "Exploited Cisco SD-WAN flaw CVE-2026-20245 turns netadmin access into root; Mandiant saw it used as a zero-day in April"
summary: "Cisco disclosed CVE-2026-20245 on 2026-06-04, a command injection in the CLI of Catalyst SD-WAN Controller, Manager and Validator that lets an authenticated local attacker with netadmin rights become root (CVSS 7.8); CISA listed it as exploited on 2026-06-09. Mandiant found it used as a zero-day in April 2026 at a service provider whose SD-WAN Manager the attacker already reached as vmanage-admin. Fixed releases are 20.9.9.2, 20.12.7.2, 20.15.4.5, 20.15.5.3, 20.18.3.1 and 26.1.1.2, with no workaround."
event_date: 2026-06-24
priority: notable
immediate_action: null
